27q1|n|A roll; a scroll; a written document rolled up for keeping or for use, after the manner of the ancients. ; Hence, a collection of printed sheets bound together, whether containing a single work, or a part of a work, or more than one work; a book; a tome; especially, that part of an extended work which is bound up together in one cover; as, a work in four volumes. ; Anything of a rounded or swelling form resembling a roll; a turn; a convolution; a coil. ; Dimensions; compass; space occupied, as measured by cubic units, that is, cubic inches, feet, yards, etc.; mass; bulk; as, the volume of an elephant's body; a volume of gas. ; Amount, fullness, quantity, or caliber of voice or tone.	a:qoz,29,2;1jda,17,3;ohj,16,4~ohj,16,4;1jda,17,3;qoz,29,2	v:qoz,19,1;1ru6,8,3;9jl,5,2~1ru6,8,3;9jl,5,2;qoz,19,1	n:9jl,32,13;qp1,30,9;1jda,17,3;1lmq,10,11;rpw,1,4~9jl,32,13;1lmq,10,11;qp1,30,9;rpw,1,4;1jda,17,3	N:14m2,72,3;a5e,67,4;1o5r,56,5;fdl,32,5;sd9,31,5~fdl,32,5;1o5r,56,5;sd9,31,5;a5e,67,4;14m2,72,3
